Quickly got a stash set up on Dlvl 3 (the only dungeon-altar in the 
whole game) and made my way to BigRoom without hassles. Gained XL 10 
there, made Sokoban for the Amulet (YAY) and then went to take out the 
mines for the luckstone. My last ascension taught me that confusion is 
important on the planes and so I started reading spellbooks so that I 
can confuse me with them later on. This proved worthy later on, but I'm 
digressing.
After the mines I had 49(!) daggers. Enchanted them to +3 and took 25 
with me, despite the insane weight. Got to Master in daggers quite soon.
Somewhen along the road i managed to tame a large dog after I found a 
magic whistle. Using a polytrap in the mines I soon had a pet marilith 
whacking anything in sight with Orcrist.
No, don't blame Orcrist on me. I got that as a first gift from Kos. 
Orcrist! Of all things, Orcrist! Oh well, I really wanted Stormy so I 
emptied a few /oCM, BoT and ?oCM on the altar. Good Trollsbane, 
Demonbane, Frost Brand and - finally Stormy. And guess what? UNCROWNED! 
All the profits of crowning without its pain! I gave Frost Brand to 
Cerberus (my pet marilith, he kept the name after the Polymorph). 
Anyway, with that equipment I descended further until XL 14 finally 
enabled me to the quest.
Having paid attention to fellow #nethack'ers I brought a cursed ?oT 
(kindly sponsored by the cursed MM (not the uncursed one I also found) 
to escape the last Quest level. Along the Quest, Cerberus (my marilith) 
died to a blue jelly which he happily slashed with Frostbrand. If I 
could have TU'd him I'd have killed him again *grr*.
Anyway, the quest it is. Using a hole I dug I landed in the Master 
Assassins part of the level, introduced him quickly to my wand of death 
and left with the MKoT.
Descending further I hit a bones of an unfortunate Barbarian who turned 
to stone by not having a lizard corpse with him. His statue donated the 
cursed +7 Cleaver and the Heart of Ahriman (which I couldn't pick up).
Tamed a horse along the way (called it Silver) and went back to the 
polytrap. Here I made an evil mistake which cost me my robe (which was 
kindly donated by the minetown priest after Cerberus (Kos bless him) had 
a short talk with him. I accidentally stepped on the polytrap myself.
Oh well, gave Frosty to the Mountain Centaur named Silver and continued 
my descent.
The Titan on Medusas got killed by late Cerberus already and Medusa 
turned herself to stone after I fell past her level and came back up 
hiding under my polished silver shield.
Perseus donated the only levitation boots I could find this game and I 
went to take out the castle. Got a 0:3 wand of wishing out of it.
Some time later I got a wand of polymorph and decided I'd try to get a 
better pet. Silver died on the first zap, leaving me with Frosty again.
Okay, finally no more care to take when running around #twoweaponing 
Stormy and a silver saber from a helpful Captain in the castle.
Found two more magic markers along the way and a second wand of wishing 
0:3 from a python in Gehennom.
In Gehennom I tamed a warhorse with a slime mold, used the polytrap I 
found to poly it into a salamder, equipped it with Orcrist (wouldn't 
pick up anything else) and some armor from the stash and went hacking 
through Gehennom.
I couldn't be bothered with the Demon Lords/Princes so I just paid them 
off where possible.
Found the VS on Dlvl 45, marked it the usual way (dug an arrow of 
holes), took out Wimp the Impaler, #enhanced Divination to Basic so I 
could cast ID and went back to the stash to create my AK.
It wasn't great, but the 4 magic markers and more than 40 cancellable 
scrolls helped a lot.
Wrote lots of ?oEA ?oEW and the four obligatory ?oDT. Two markers dried 
out to 1:0 so I stashed them away. Wished up speed boots and a HoB.
Back down to Rodney, killed him with a /oD before he realized what hit 
him (didn't even pick up the Book) and made a run for the VS.
Silver II (the salamander) seems to have gone back through the portal 
into Rodneys tower, at least he was there when I left it and wasn't seen 
anymore after that. I didn't bother searching for him.
The High Priest of Moloch committed suicide by zapping his /oD at my 
amulet of reflection. I gladly took the Amulet and made a run for the 
planes.
Only a single mysterious force and two Rodney appearences (plus the one 
on the Plane of Earth) which were taken care of by whacking him (first 
time) and /oD (second and third time).
Quickly reblessed all equipment at the stash (where 20 holy water were 
waiting) and left for the planes with 2 /oDig in my bag.
On Earth only 4 charges of a /oDig were necessary.
On Air conflict helped me evading most anything. Didn't even get 
swallowed once.
On Fire the same was happening.
On Water I removed the =oConflict and Amulet of Reflection, ended 
#twoweaponing, wilded Stormy and put on a shield of reflection and the 
Amulet of Yendor for the hot/cold game.
Some time in between I confused me and read a ?oGD to see where the ^ 
was. To my surprise it was still visible some time later! I thought it 
would vanish from visibility again. Happily jumped in.
On Astral I quickly took care of an arch-lich and took a few !oFH out of 
my oilskin bag and dropped it. All those stuff I took out of the BoH 
earlier got me burdened which was unfavorable on Astral. I dropped the 
oilskin bag with some holy water, !oFH and ?oRC, wished for a cockatrice 
corpse, put on levitation boots, =oFA and =oConflict and ran for the 
left altar. Famine was waiting for me there. I switched to +7 Stormy and 
+6 silver saber and Famine was down in 2 turns. Using the cockatrice 
corpse I stoned my way through to the altar and it was really Kos altar!
Right on first try! I lit the Candelabrum for style and sacced the amulet!

